        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(nostr): keep profile imports as cancellable drafts",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nNostr profile imports could mutate config before the user reviewed relay data. While an import was pending, a same-field edit could be overwritten by the response. Cancel could close the form while a server-side merge still persisted.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe Control UI now requests `autoMerge: false`, treats relay data as a draft, locks profile controls while importing, and aborts/invalidate imports on Cancel, disconnect, or form replacement. Late responses cannot update a hidden or newer form. Explicit **Save & Publish** remains the write path.\n\nThe existing HTTP contract is preserved: callers that explicitly send `autoMerge: true` retain server-side merge and persistence. Only the Control UI opts into draft mode.\n\n## User Impact\n\nImported values fill the open form for review. Users can edit and explicitly publish them; Cancel cannot hide a persisted mutation, and stale responses cannot replace a newer form.\n\n## Evidence\n\n### Real Control UI + relay/browser proof\n\nA standalone Chromium run drove the actual Control UI. Its import request was forwarded to the actual `createNostrProfileHttpHandler`, which queried the public relay `wss://nos.lol`. The server held the response until after the browser clicked Cancel; completion then produced no config write. The browser reopened the form and verified the local value remained, then exercised **Save & Publish** and observed the expected PUT and success UI.\n\nRedacted output:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"browser\": \"Chromium\",\n  \"relay\": \"wss://nos.lol\",\n  \"pubkeyPrefix\": \"c938f0bd…\",\n  \"relayPublish\": \"accepted\",\n  \"pendingImport\": { \"browserRequest\": { \"autoMerge\": false }, \"fieldsDisabled\": true },\n  \"cancel\": {\n    \"clientAction\": \"Cancel\",\n    \"serverCompletedAfterCancel\": true,\n    \"serverPersistenceCalls\": 0,\n    \"persistedProfile\": { \"name\": \"local\" },\n    \"formValueAfterReopen\": \"local\",\n    \"requestWasDelayedUntilCancel\": true\n  },\n  \"saveAndPublish\": {\n    \"requestMethod\": \"PUT\",\n    \"requestBody\": { \"name\": \"saved-draft\" },\n    \"uiSuccess\": true\n  }\n}\n```\n\nThe run generated pending-import, after-Cancel/reopen, and after-Save screenshots plus a Chromium WebM recording under `.artifacts/control-ui-e2e/nostr-live-proof/`. The browser run was against the same implementation before the final rebase; the final rebases only added current-main commits outside this PR’s changed paths.\n\n### CI/base diagnosis and focused validation\n\n- The earlier Apple i18n failure (`checks-node-compact-small-2`, run `29220125349`) was on old base `f26793ca54`; the PR never touched `apps/ios/Sources/Design/SettingsProTabSections.swift`. Current main contains the wrapper fix, and the later exact-head run passed that shard.\n- Exact-head run `29220974456` identified the branch-specific guard failure: `ui/src/pages/channels/channels-page.ts` grew from 514 to 538 lines. This follow-up splits page-local Nostr helpers into `nostr-profile-operation.ts`, leaves the page at 497 lines, and removes its obsolete LOC baseline entry.\n- The same exact-head run’s dependency failure listed only existing `src/agents/*` and `src/gateway/*` unused-export ratchet entries; no changed PR path was listed. Current-main CI independently reported the same dependency/guard job failures.\n- Final base at last sync: `b43e832fcc8000ed7287c7accc54e381db607f85`.\n- `OPENCLAW_VITEST_MAX_WORKERS=1 node_modules/.bin/vitest run extensions/nostr/src/nostr-profile-http.test.ts extensions/nostr/src/nostr-profile-import.test.ts` — 34 tests passed.\n- `OPENCLAW_VITEST_MAX_WORKERS=1 node_modules/.bin/vitest run ui/src/pages/channels/channels-page.test.ts ui/src/pages/channels/view.test.ts` — 14 tests passed.\n- `OPENCLAW_VITEST_MAX_WORKERS=1 node_modules/.bin/vitest run --config test/vitest/vitest.ui-e2e.config.ts --configLoader runner ui/src/e2e/nostr-profile-import.e2e.test.ts` — 1 Playwright test passed.\n- Scoped `oxfmt` and `oxlint` passed for the changed UI and Nostr files.\n\n## Limitations\n\nThe browser Save & Publish evidence uses the UI’s PUT request with a deterministic successful response; it does not claim a live publish from a running Nostr bus. The HTTP persistence path remains covered by focused handler tests. The live import/Cancel path uses a public relay and the actual HTTP handler in a real local HTTP runtime.\n\nCrabbox was attempted but unavailable for this run: AWS had no usable credential/instance role, and the DigitalOcean provider required `DIGITALOCEAN_TOKEN` in the environment. No token was copied from chat and no remote lease was created; provider: local Chromium/direct local fallback, lease: N/A.\n\nAI-assisted: built and reviewed with Codex.\n",
        "branch": "fix/nostr-import-draft-race",
